# 318: §2 pins `x = (y = 1)` as a PARSE error — `=` is a statement token, not an
# expression operator, and an engine that accepted it would diverge from one that
# did not. Wording follows error.rs `unexpected_token`, whose own doc names this
# exact program: "unexpected <token>", the token spelled by Display for
# TokenKind and quoted. Nothing runs, so there is no output.
--- source
let x = 1;
let y = 2;
x = (y = 1);
--- expect
error: Parse at line 3: unexpected '='
